-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Spellbound Dizzy
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1991
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        Dizzy V - Spellbound Dizzy (1991)(Codemasters)[a].z80
  MD5         703c934aa64c1c1d37d5041dd28cf9c7

  File        Dizzy V - Spellbound Dizzy (1991)(Codemasters).z80
  MD5         0b7078da25eaa0e50d679ae03f9f99ff

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Note        Dizzy is hardware sprites, so he no longer takes the colours of
              the scenery he walks through; the rooms, the items and the
              dialogue boxes stay as the game draws them. The 48K release.
              Starts from the game itself, past its BASIC loader. Proven on
              recorded play of the first rooms and dialogue; the inventory and
              a lost life are not in the recordings.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite stars

  Infinite lives and Infinite stars from an archive .pok, checked against this
  release's code (the lives counter's DEC and the star count's SUB). The
  archive's immunity cheats fit a different release and are left out.

